{"task_id": "Mbpp/12", "solution": "import collections\ndef sort_matrix(matrix):\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts a given matrix in ascending order according to the sum of its rows.\n    Uses a stable sort by creating (row_sum, original_row) pairs.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not matrix:\n        return []\n\n    # Create a list of tuples: (sum_of_row, original_row)\n    # This preserves the original row for sorting and subsequent extraction\n    row_sums_and_rows = []\n    for row in matrix:\n        row_sums_and_rows.append((sum(row), row))\n\n    # Sort the list of tuples based on the sum of the row (the first element of the tuple).\n    # Python's built-in `sorted` is stable, which means it preserves the original order\n    # for elements with equal keys.\n    sorted_row_sums_and_rows = sorted(row_sums_and_rows, key=lambda x: x[0])\n\n    # Extract the original rows from the sorted list of tuples\n    sorted_matrix = [row for _, row in sorted_row_sums_and_rows]\n\n    return sorted_matrix"}
