{"task_id": "Mbpp/65", "solution": "def recursive_list_sum(input_list):\n    \"\"\"\n    Flattens a list and sums all of its numeric elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    def _is_numeric(element):\n        \"\"\"Checks if an element is an integer or a float.\"\"\"\n        return isinstance(element, (int, float))\n\n    def _flatten_list(nested_list):\n        \"\"\"Recursively flattens a nested list.\"\"\"\n        flattened = []\n        for item in nested_list:\n            if isinstance(item, list):\n                flattened.extend(_flatten_list(item))\n            else:\n                flattened.append(item)\n        return flattened\n\n    flattened_elements = _flatten_list(input_list)\n    total_sum = 0\n    for element in flattened_elements:\n        if _is_numeric(element):\n            total_sum += element\n    return total_sum"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/63", "solution": "from typing import List, Tuple, Union\n\ndef max_difference(tuple_list: List[Tuple[Union[int, float], Union[int, float]]]) -> Union[int, float]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the maximum absolute difference between pairs in a list of tuples.\n    Assumes valid input where each tuple contains exactly two numeric elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    current_max_diff = 0.0\n\n    for a, b in tuple_list:\n        diff = abs(a - b)\n        if diff > current_max_diff:\n            current_max_diff = diff\n            \n    return current_max_diff"}
