{"task_id": "Mbpp/68", "solution": "def is_Monotonic(array):\n    \"\"\"\n    Check whether the given array is monotonic or not.\n    An array is monotonic if it is either entirely non-decreasing\n    or entirely non-increasing.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(array) <= 1:\n        return True\n\n    increasing = False\n    decreasing = False\n\n    for i in range(1, len(array)):\n        if array[i] > array[i-1]:\n            increasing = True\n        elif array[i] < array[i-1]:\n            decreasing = True\n\n        if increasing and decreasing:\n            return False\n\n    return True"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/69", "solution": "def is_sublist(main_list, sublist):\n    \"\"\"\n    Check if sublist appears as consecutive elements in main_list.\n    Raises TypeError if inputs are not lists.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(main_list, list) or not isinstance(sublist, list):\n        raise TypeError(\"Both main_list and sublist must be of type list.\")\n\n    n = len(main_list)\n    m = len(sublist)\n\n    if m == 0:\n        return True\n    if m > n:\n        return False\n\n    for i in range(n - m + 1):\n        if main_list[i:i + m] == sublist:\n            return True\n    return False"}
