{"task_id": "Mbpp/103", "solution": "def eulerian_num(n, m):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the Eulerian number a(n, m).\n    This function uses a recursive formula with memoization to ensure efficiency.\n    \"\"\"\n    if m < 0 or m >= n:\n        return 0\n    if n == 0 and m == 0:\n        return 1\n    if n == 1 and m == 0:\n        return 1\n    \n    # Using a dictionary for memoization to store previously computed values\n    # The key is a tuple (n, m)\n    memo = {}\n\n    def _eulerian_recursive(n_val, m_val):\n        if (n_val, m_val) in memo:\n            return memo[(n_val, m_val)]\n\n        if m_val < 0 or m_val >= n_val:\n            return 0\n        if n_val == 0 and m_val == 0:\n            return 1\n        # Base case for n=1\n        if n_val == 1 and m_val == 0:\n            return 1\n\n        # Recursive formula: A(n, m) = (m+1)A(n-1, m) + (n-m)A(n-1, m-1)\n        result = (m_val + 1) * _eulerian_recursive(n_val - 1, m_val) + \\\n                 (n_val - m_val) * _eulerian_recursive(n_val - 1, m_val - 1)\n        \n        memo[(n_val, m_val)] = result\n        return result\n\n    return _eulerian_recursive(n, m)"}
