{"task_id": "Mbpp/123", "solution": "import math\n\ndef sum_of_proper_divisors(number: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of proper divisors of a given number.\n    Returns 0 for numbers less than or equal to 1.\"\"\"\n    if number <= 1:\n        return 0\n    s = 1  # 1 is always a proper divisor for numbers greater than 1\n    # Iterate from 2 up to the square root of the number\n    for i in range(2, int(math.sqrt(number)) + 1):\n        if number % i == 0:\n            s += i\n            # If i*i is not equal to number, then number // i is another distinct divisor\n            if i * i != number:\n                s += number // i\n    return s\n\ndef amicable_numbers_sum(upper_limit: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Sums all amicable numbers from 1 to a specified upper_limit.\"\"\"\n    amicable_set = set()\n    divisor_sums_cache = {}  # Cache to store sum_of_proper_divisors results\n\n    for n in range(1, upper_limit + 1):\n        if n in amicable_set:\n            continue  # This number has already been identified and added to the set\n\n        # Calculate d1, the sum of proper divisors for n\n        if n in divisor_sums_cache:\n            d1 = divisor_sums_cache[n]\n        else:\n            d1 = sum_of_proper_divisors(n)\n            divisor_sums_cache[n] = d1\n        \n        # Check for potential amicable pair (n, d1)\n        # Conditions: d1 must be greater than n (to avoid duplicates and self-pairs)\n        # and d1 must be greater than 1 (as d(1)=0 which cannot form a pair).\n        if d1 > n and d1 > 1:\n            # Calculate d2, the sum of proper divisors for d1\n            if d1 in divisor_sums_cache:\n                d2 = divisor_sums_cache[d1]\n            else:\n                d2 = sum_of_proper_divisors(d1)\n                divisor_sums_cache[d1] = d2\n            \n            # If d2 equals n, then (n, d1) is an amicable pair\n            if d2 == n:\n                # Add both numbers to the set if they are within the specified upper_limit\n                if n <= upper_limit:\n                    amicable_set.add(n)\n                if d1 <= upper_limit:\n                    amicable_set.add(d1)\n    \n    return sum(amicable_set)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/126", "solution": "def find_divisors(n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds all positive divisors of a given integer.\n    Includes 1 and the number itself.\n    \"\"\"\n    divs = []\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        if n % i == 0:\n            divs.append(i)\n    return divs\n\ndef find_common_divisors(divisors1, divisors2):\n    \"\"\"\n    Identifies common divisors between two lists of divisors.\n    Uses set intersection for efficient comparison.\n    \"\"\"\n    return list(set(divisors1) & set(divisors2))\n\ndef calculate_sum(divisors):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of all numbers in a given list.\n    \"\"\"\n    return sum(divisors)\n\ndef sum(a, b):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of common divisors of two given numbers.\n    Orchestrates finding divisors, common divisors, and their sum.\n    \"\"\"\n    divisors_a = find_divisors(a)\n    divisors_b = find_divisors(b)\n    common_divs = find_common_divisors(divisors_a, divisors_b)\n    return calculate_sum(common_divs)"}
