{"task_id": "Mbpp/137", "solution": "def zero_count(array: list[int]) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the ratio of zeroes to non-zeroes in an array of integers.\n    Handles edge cases where non-zero count is zero.\n    \"\"\"\n    zero_count_val = 0\n    non_zero_count_val = 0\n\n    for x in array:\n        if x == 0:\n            zero_count_val += 1\n        else:\n            non_zero_count_val += 1\n\n    if non_zero_count_val == 0:\n        # According to UC-004, this should return float('inf') or similar.\n        # Python's default float division by zero returns float('inf') for positive numerator,\n        # which is appropriate here.\n        return float(zero_count_val) / non_zero_count_val\n    else:\n        return float(zero_count_val) / non_zero_count_val"}
