{"task_id": "Mbpp/141", "solution": "def pancake_sort(arr: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts a list of elements using the pancake sort algorithm.\n    Returns a new list with elements in ascending order.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n    # Create a copy to avoid modifying the original list in place\n    sorted_arr = arr.copy()\n\n    # Helper function to reverse a sub-array from 0 to 'index'\n    def _flip(sub_arr: list, index: int) -> None:\n        start = 0\n        while start < index:\n            sub_arr[start], sub_arr[index] = sub_arr[index], sub_arr[start]\n            start += 1\n            index -= 1\n\n    # Helper function to find the index of the maximum element in a sub-array\n    def _find_max_index(sub_arr: list, end: int) -> int:\n        max_val = sub_arr[0]\n        max_idx = 0\n        for i in range(1, end + 1):\n            if sub_arr[i] > max_val:\n                max_val = sub_arr[i]\n                max_idx = i\n        return max_idx\n\n    # Iterate from the current size of the unsorted part down to 1\n    for curr_size in range(n, 1, -1):\n        # Find the index of the maximum element in the current unsorted segment\n        max_idx = _find_max_index(sorted_arr, curr_size - 1)\n\n        # If the maximum element is not already at its correct position\n        if max_idx != curr_size - 1:\n            # If the maximum element is not at the beginning, flip to bring it to index 0\n            if max_idx != 0:\n                _flip(sorted_arr, max_idx)\n            # Flip the entire current unsorted segment to move the maximum element to its final position\n            _flip(sorted_arr, curr_size - 1)\n            \n    return sorted_arr"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/145", "solution": "def max_Abs_Diff(array):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the maximum absolute difference between any two elements in a given array.\n    This is achieved by subtracting the minimum element from the maximum element.\n    \"\"\"\n    min_val = min(array)\n    max_val = max(array)\n    return max_val - min_val"}
