{"task_id": "Mbpp/235", "solution": "def even_bit_set_number(number: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sets all even-positioned bits (0, 2, 4, etc.) to 1 in the given number.\n    Uses a bitwise OR operation with a mask that has 1s at even bit positions.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Create an even bit mask. 0x5555... has 1s at even positions (0, 2, 4, ...).\n    # Since Python integers have arbitrary precision, we use a sufficiently large mask.\n    # This mask covers up to 64 bits.\n    even_bit_mask = 0x5555555555555555\n    # Apply the mask using a bitwise OR operation to set all even bits to 1.\n    return number | even_bit_mask"}
