{"task_id": "Mbpp/247", "solution": "def lps(s: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the length of the longest palindromic subsequence in the given string using dynamic programming.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(s)\n\n    # Base cases for empty or single-character strings\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    if n == 1:\n        return 1\n\n    # Create a 2D DP table to store results of subproblems.\n    # dp[i][j] stores the length of the longest palindromic subsequence of s[i...j].\n    dp = [[0] * n for _ in range(n)]\n\n    # All single characters are palindromes of length 1.\n    for i in range(n):\n        dp[i][i] = 1\n\n    # Fill the DP table.\n    # 'length' represents the length of the current substring (from 2 up to n).\n    for length in range(2, n + 1):\n        for i in range(n - length + 1):\n            j = i + length - 1  # 'j' is the end index of the current substring s[i...j].\n\n            # If characters at the ends match, they can be part of the palindrome.\n            # Add 2 to the LPS of the inner substring s[i+1...j-1].\n            if s[i] == s[j]:\n                dp[i][j] = 2 + dp[i + 1][j - 1]\n            # If characters at the ends do not match, we must exclude one of them.\n            # Take the maximum of LPS of s[i+1...j] (excluding s[i]) and s[i...j-1] (excluding s[j]).\n            else:\n                dp[i][j] = max(dp[i + 1][j], dp[i][j - 1])\n\n    # The value dp[0][n-1] will contain the length of the longest palindromic subsequence\n    # for the entire string s.\n    return dp[0][n - 1]"}
