{"task_id": "Mbpp/264", "solution": "def dog_age(human_age: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates a dog's age in dog years using a piecewise linear conversion formula.\n    The first year converts to 15 dog years, the second to 9, and subsequent years to 5 each.\n    \"\"\"\n    if human_age <= 0:\n        return 0\n    elif human_age == 1:\n        return 15\n    elif human_age == 2:\n        return 15 + 9\n    else:\n        # For human_age greater than 2:\n        # The first two years contribute 15 + 9 = 24 dog years.\n        # Each year after the second contributes 5 dog years.\n        return 15 + 9 + (human_age - 2) * 5"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/265", "solution": "def list_split(input_list: list, n: int) -> list[list]:\n    \"\"\"Splits a list into n sublists using a round-robin distribution.\n    Each element at index `i` in the original list is placed into sublist `i % n`.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"n must be a positive integer.\")\n\n    # Initialize n empty sublists\n    result_lists = [[] for _ in range(n)]\n\n    # Distribute elements in a round-robin fashion\n    for i, item in enumerate(input_list):\n        result_lists[i % n].append(item)\n\n    return result_lists"}
