{"task_id": "Mbpp/285", "solution": "def text_match_two_three(input_string: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Check if string contains 'a' followed by exactly 2 or 3 'b' characters.\n\n    Args:\n        input_string (str): The string to analyze\n\n    Returns:\n        bool: True if pattern 'abb' or 'abbb' found, False otherwise\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(input_string)\n    for i in range(n):\n        if input_string[i] == 'a':\n            # Check for 'abb' pattern\n            if i + 2 < n and input_string[i+1] == 'b' and input_string[i+2] == 'b':\n                # 'abb' found, now check the exact count of 'b's\n                if i + 3 < n and input_string[i+3] == 'b':\n                    # We have at least 'abbb'. Now ensure it's not 'abbbb' or longer.\n                    if i + 4 < n and input_string[i+4] == 'b':\n                        # Found 'abbbb', which is not allowed. Continue searching.\n                        continue\n                    else:\n                        # Found 'abbb' and no fourth 'b'. This is a match.\n                        return True\n                else:\n                    # Found 'abb' and no third 'b'. This is a match.\n                    return True\n    return False"}
