{"task_id": "Mbpp/409", "solution": "def min_product_tuple(tuples: list) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the minimum product from pairs of tuples within a given list.\n    Validates input and computes products to find the smallest value.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _validate_input(data: list):\n        \"\"\"Validates the input list for emptiness and tuple structure.\"\"\"\n        if not data:\n            raise ValueError(\"Input list cannot be empty.\")\n        for item in data:\n            if not isinstance(item, tuple) or len(item) != 2:\n                raise ValueError(\"Each item in the list must be a tuple of exactly two elements.\")\n            if not all(isinstance(x, (int, float)) for x in item):\n                raise ValueError(\"Tuple elements must be numeric (int or float).\")\n\n    def _calculate_products(data: list) -> list:\n        \"\"\"Calculates the product of elements for each tuple in the list.\"\"\"\n        return [item[0] * item[1] for item in data]\n\n    def _find_minimum(products: list) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Finds the minimum value from a list of products.\"\"\"\n        if not products:\n            # This case should ideally be caught by _validate_input for non-empty list,\n            # but as a safeguard or if requirements change for empty input to return something else.\n            raise ValueError(\"No products to find minimum from.\")\n        return min(products)\n\n    _validate_input(tuples)\n    products_list = _calculate_products(tuples)\n    return _find_minimum(products_list)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/410", "solution": "def _filter_numeric_values(input_list: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Filters a list to include only numeric (int or float) values.\"\"\"\n    numeric_values = []\n    for item in input_list:\n        if isinstance(item, (int, float)):\n            numeric_values.append(item)\n    return numeric_values\n\ndef min_val(input_list: list) -> int | float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the minimum numeric value in a given heterogeneous list.\n    Raises ValueError if no numeric values are found in the list.\n    \"\"\"\n    numeric_values = _filter_numeric_values(input_list)\n\n    if not numeric_values:\n        raise ValueError(\"No numeric values found in the list.\")\n\n    return min(numeric_values)"}
