{"task_id": "Mbpp/413", "solution": "def _validate_input(tuple_list, index):\n    \"\"\"\n    Validates input parameters for extract_nth_element function.\n    Raises TypeError if parameters are wrong type, ValueError if index is negative.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(tuple_list, list):\n        raise TypeError(\"tuple_list must be a list.\")\n    if not isinstance(index, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"index must be an integer.\")\n    if index < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"index must be a non-negative integer.\")\n\ndef extract_nth_element(tuple_list, index):\n    \"\"\"\n    Extract the nth element from each tuple in the given list.\n    Returns a new list containing extracted elements in original order.\n    \"\"\"\n    _validate_input(tuple_list, index)\n    \n    result = []\n    for tup in tuple_list:\n        result.append(tup[index])\n            \n    return result"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/415", "solution": "def max_Product(array: list[int]) -> tuple[int, int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds a pair of integers with the highest product from a given array.\n    The returned tuple will have the smaller number first.\n    \"\"\"\n    sorted_arr = sorted(array)\n    n = len(sorted_arr)\n\n    # Calculate product of the two smallest numbers (potential for high positive product if both are negative)\n    product1 = sorted_arr[0] * sorted_arr[1]\n    pair1 = (sorted_arr[0], sorted_arr[1])\n\n    # Calculate product of the two largest numbers\n    product2 = sorted_arr[n-2] * sorted_arr[n-1]\n    pair2 = (sorted_arr[n-2], sorted_arr[n-1])\n\n    if product1 > product2:\n        return pair1\n    else:\n        return pair2"}
