{"task_id": "Mbpp/436", "solution": "def validate_input(input_list: list) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Ensures input is a valid list structure.\n    Per instructions, this function assumes valid list input without using `isinstance`.\"\"\"\n    return True\n\ndef is_negative(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Determines if a given number is negative.\"\"\"\n    return number < 0\n\ndef collect_negatives(input_list: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Assembles filtered results maintaining original order.\"\"\"\n    negative_numbers = []\n    for item in input_list:\n        if is_negative(item):\n            negative_numbers.append(item)\n    return negative_numbers\n\ndef neg_nos(input_list: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns the negative numbers in a list, preserving their original order.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not validate_input(input_list):\n        return []\n\n    return collect_negatives(input_list)"}
