{"task_id": "Mbpp/468", "solution": "from typing import List\n\ndef max_product(arr: List[float]) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the maximum product formed by multiplying numbers of an increasing subsequence.\n    Uses dynamic programming to track the maximum product ending at each element.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0.0\n\n    # dp[i] stores the maximum product of an increasing subsequence ending with arr[i].\n    dp = [0.0] * n\n\n    # Initialize max_product_val to negative infinity to handle arrays with negative numbers correctly.\n    max_product_val = float('-inf')\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        # An increasing subsequence can always be formed by just the element itself.\n        dp[i] = float(arr[i])\n\n        # Iterate through previous elements to find potential predecessors.\n        for j in range(i):\n            if arr[j] < arr[i]:\n                # If arr[j] can precede arr[i], try extending the subsequence ending at arr[j].\n                dp[i] = max(dp[i], dp[j] * arr[i])\n\n        # Update the overall maximum product found so far.\n        max_product_val = max(max_product_val, dp[i])\n\n    return max_product_val"}
