{"task_id": "Mbpp/581", "solution": "import math\n\ndef surface_Area(base_edge, height):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the surface area of a square pyramid given its base edge and perpendicular height.\n    The total area is the sum of the base area and the four triangular face areas.\n    \"\"\"\n    base_area = base_edge ** 2\n    \n    # Calculate the slant height using the Pythagorean theorem\n    half_base_edge = base_edge / 2\n    slant_height = math.sqrt(height**2 + half_base_edge**2)\n    \n    # Calculate the area of one triangular face\n    triangular_face_area = 0.5 * base_edge * slant_height\n    \n    # The total surface area is the base area plus four times the triangular face area\n    total_surface_area = base_area + 4 * triangular_face_area\n    \n    return total_surface_area"}
