{"task_id": "Mbpp/598", "solution": "def armstrong_number(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a number is an Armstrong number.\n    An Armstrong number is equal to the sum of its digits, each raised to the power of the number of digits.\n    \"\"\"\n    if number < 0:\n        return False\n    \n    num_str = str(number)\n    num_digits = len(num_str)\n    \n    sum_of_powers = 0\n    temp_num = number\n    \n    while temp_num > 0:\n        digit = temp_num % 10\n        sum_of_powers += digit ** num_digits\n        temp_num //= 10\n        \n    return sum_of_powers == number"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/602", "solution": "def first_repeated_char(s: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Find the first repeated character in a string.\n    Returns the first character that appears more than once, or None if no repetition.\n    \"\"\"\n    seen_chars = set()\n    for char in s:\n        if char in seen_chars:\n            return char\n        seen_chars.add(char)\n    return None"}
