{"task_id": "Mbpp/739", "solution": "def find_Index(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the index of the smallest triangular number that has exactly n digits.\n    It iterates through triangular numbers, counting digits until the target count is met.\n    \"\"\"\n    k = 1\n    while True:\n        triangular_number = k * (k + 1) // 2\n        \n        # Count digits of the triangular number\n        digit_count = len(str(triangular_number))\n        \n        if digit_count == n:\n            return k\n        \n        k += 1"}
