{"task_id": "Mbpp/743", "solution": "def rotate_right(lst, positions):\n    \"\"\"\n    Rotate a list to the right by specified number of positions.\n    Returns a new list with elements rotated to the right.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not lst:\n        return []\n    \n    n = len(lst)\n    effective_positions = positions % n\n    \n    # Slice the list into two parts and concatenate them in reverse order\n    # The last 'effective_positions' elements move to the front\n    # The remaining elements follow\n    return lst[-effective_positions:] + lst[:-effective_positions]"}
